5. Comparison of MySQL, PostgreSQL, Oracle, and SQLite

MySQL is one of the most popular relational database management systems. It is widely used in web applications, e-commerce websites, and content management systems because it is easy to learn, fast, and reliable.

PostgreSQL is an advanced open-source database system known for its powerful features and support for complex queries. It is commonly used in enterprise applications, analytics platforms, and systems requiring high data integrity.

Oracle Database is an enterprise-level database management system used by large organizations such as banks, healthcare institutions, and government agencies. It offers excellent security, scalability, and performance for mission-critical applications.

SQLite is a lightweight, serverless database engine that stores data in a single file. It is commonly used in mobile applications, desktop software, embedded systems, and Internet of Things (IoT) devices because it requires minimal setup and maintenance.

Conclusion

This assignment demonstrated the installation and use of MySQL Workbench, creation of databases and tables, insertion of data, establishment of relationships using foreign keys, and comparison of popular database management systems. The InstaClone database successfully models a simple social media application with users and posts connected through a relational database structure.


