3. LOOP Example: Print Numbers 1 to 5

The following PL/SQL block uses a simple LOOP and EXIT WHEN condition.

```sql
DECLARE
    v_counter NUMBER := 1;
BEGIN
    LOOP
        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(v_counter);
        v_counter := v_counter + 1;

        EXIT WHEN v_counter > 5;
    END LOOP;
END;
/
```

Output:

```
1
2
3
4
5
```

4. Cursor Example

The following PL/SQL block declares a cursor to fetch product names from the PRODUCTS table and print them.

```sql
DECLARE
    CURSOR product_cursor IS
        SELECT PRODUCT_NAME
        FROM PRODUCTS;

    v_product_name PRODUCTS.PRODUCT_NAME%TYPE;
BEGIN
    OPEN product_cursor;

    LOOP
        FETCH product_cursor INTO v_product_name;
        EXIT WHEN product_cursor%NOTFOUND;

        DBMS_OUTPUT.PUT_LINE(v_product_name);
    END LOOP;

    CLOSE product_cursor;
END;
/
```

Sample Output:

```
Laptop
Mouse
Keyboard
Monitor
Printer
```

